  "comment": "The notifier's pure parts (D153, D191): addresses is an address normalised by its kind (TypeScript's normaliseAddress, Rust's normalise_address); replies is a reply's words read (readReply, read_reply) and whether its text is shaped as a code (looksLikeCode, looks_like_code); quietHours is how many seconds a wall time waits out quiet hours (quietDelaySeconds at an instant in a zone, whose wall time is wall, and Rust's quiet_delay_seconds of the wall time); quietHoursAcrossChanges is the same on nights the clocks change inside the window, from an instant in a zone (quietDelaySeconds, Go's QuietDelayAt); trust is a channel's trust over a principal's permissions (replyAllows, reply_allows; narrowedPermissions, narrowed_permissions), a null cap no cap; codeHashes is a code's stored hash (codeHash, code_hash); sameIds is an id in one form (sameId, same_id). runtime/http/typescript's notify-parity.test.ts writes the wants with NOTIFY_PARITY_WRITE=1.",
